# Tidy on the Today divider needs something a run could do (Pane, 14 Nov 2026): one tab alone has
# nothing to group, and tabs all in sections made by hand (Add Only: Tidy may only add to them) leave
# nothing to offer the model, so the divider shows no Tidy, not even with Shift over it. A second loose
# tab is enough (with Shift, under eleven Today tabs). tabGroups= reads what the divider is told,
# divider= the row itself; dividerShift= stands in for the Shift key, hover= for the pointer.
budget rss=800 stalls50=30
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
env CRA_TIDY_FAKE_MODEL=1
pace 0.2

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=1
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?tabGroups=one
expect-log tab groups one: +tidy=hidden$
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=2
wait 1
cra://debug?tabGroups=two
expect-log tab groups two: +tidy=withShift$
# Both into a section made by hand: nothing Tidy may sort, not even with Shift.
cra://debug?newSection=Mine&tabs=2
wait 0.5
cra://debug?tabGroups=byHand
expect-log tab groups byHand: Mine\(open rows=2/2\) tidy=hidden$
cra://debug?dividerShift=1
cra://debug?hover=DividerRowView
cra://debug?divider=byHandShift
expect-log divider byHandShift: tidy=none button=0 hovered=1$
cra://debug?dividerShift=auto
reject-log fault:
